  "synonym_discrimination": null,
  "usage_note": "**A little** is a little more formal than **a bit**, which means the same in speech: *a bit tired*. Before an uncountable noun, **a little** is a determiner (*a little water*), a separate entry under **little**.",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "I'm little tired.",
      "correct": "I'm a little tired.",
      "note": "**Little** alone cannot go before an ordinary adjective such as **tired**; it needs **a**."
